TACO STAMPEDE

FORMAT (HARD LOCKS)
Duration: 25 seconds
Aspect Ratio: 9:16 (vertical)
FPS: 48
Genre: Prehistoric stampede / absurd apex-predator realism
Max shot length: 1.2s
Avg shot length: 0.6–0.9s

ABSOLUTE RULE ZERO

NO IDLE STATES
NO STATIC ROARS
NO POSED INTIMIDATION
NO ESTABLISHING SHOTS

Anchor image visible at 0.00s, already in motion.
If any T-rex appears stationary for more than 0.2s, force immediate forward movement or cut.

🦖 PRIMARY SUBJECT — TACO T-REX PACK (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

Always in continuous locomotion.
Walking, surging, splashing, pivoting, downhill charging, brushing past trees.
Center of mass always shifting forward.
Roars may occur only while moving.
No upright display poses.
No stop-and-stare behavior.
This is a moving herd, not a single posing monster.

🎥 CAMERA LAW (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

Camera behaves like a wildlife crew caught inside the stampede.
Mechanically linked to footfalls and near-misses.

Each major footstep causes:

lateral sway

vertical shock

shallow water vibration

rolling parallax through trunks and moss

Camera may never fully stabilize while T-rex is visible.
Constant motion only: low tracking, side rushes, retreating handheld, near-collision whip-pans, brush occlusions, creek-edge glides.
No decorative shake. All motion must come from terrain, footfalls, or evasive repositioning.

🌿 ENVIRONMENT RULES

Dense moss-covered forest ravine with shallow creek, wet stones, exposed roots, hanging lichen, narrow animal-path geometry.

Every T-rex step must cause environmental consequence:

creek water bursts upward

mud kicks back

roots flex or tear

bark scrapes off trunks

hanging moss shakes loose

loose stones tumble into water

brush folds and snaps under mass

If the environment does not react, the shot is invalid.

🌮 TACO BIOLOGY RULES

Taco shells are mounted across the back like absurd biological armor or ceremonial cresting.
They must react physically to motion:

shells rattle under gait shock

lettuce whips in air drag

salsa flecks loose on impacts

meat shifts under inertia

crema or sauce smears with vibration

fillings bounce but remain largely attached

Treat the tacos as part of the creature’s silhouette and momentum, not as static props.

🧠 VISUAL LANGUAGE

Tone is dead serious.
No comedy mugging.
No cartoon behavior.
No stylized VFX overlays.
Absurdity comes only from treating the image as real nature footage.

Visual emphasis:

kinetic realism

shallow depth of field

near-lens splashes

moss/branch occlusion

jawline danger

pack momentum

biological absurdity played straight

